<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-11.50%" pitch="-2.90%">
      The Lord calls Samuel a third time.<break time="1000ms"/>
      "Samuel."<break time="1800ms"/>

      And a third time the boy rises and goes to Eli.<break time="500ms"/>
      "Here I am," he says, "for you called me."<break time="1800ms"/>

      But this time something shifts in the old priest's understanding.<break time="500ms"/>
      Eli perceives that it is the Lord who is calling the boy.<break time="1000ms"/>
      His dim eyes may not see well, but his heart recognizes what is happening.<break time="1800ms"/>

      So Eli tells Samuel what to do.<break time="500ms"/>
      "Go, lie down," he says.<break time="500ms"/>
      "And if he calls you, you shall say, 'Speak, Lord, for your servant hears.'"<break time="1800ms"/>

      It is such a simple instruction.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not complicated.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not frightening.<break time="500ms"/>
      Just an old man helping a young boy know how to respond to the voice of God.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Sometimes we need someone beside us to help us understand what we are hearing.<break time="500ms"/>
      Someone who has walked longer in the ways of God.<break time="500ms"/>
      Someone who can say, gently, "That voice you hear is not mine. It belongs to the Lord."<break time="1800ms"/>

      Samuel goes back to his place.<break time="500ms"/>
      He lies down in the dark.<break time="500ms"/>
      The lamp of God burns low above him.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And now he knows what to say if the voice comes again.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He waits.<break time="500ms"/>
      He listens.<break time="500ms"/>
      He is ready.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
